  "repeats": [],
  "notes": [
   "Parts are unchanged from step 1.",
   "Breadboard holes are read from the circuit image. The LED sits in the image's top half (rows f-j), which I mapped to bank 'b' using the row letters. Its legs R, COM, G, B are in columns 9, 10, 11, 12 of row g.",
   "Each 220 ohm resistor spans the centre gap in columns 9, 11 and 12. Its top-half leg is in row f and its bottom-half leg in row e (banks 'b' and 't').",
   "The 5V wire ends in 10b.f. This is the same strip as the LED's COM (longest) leg, so 5V reaches the common anode.",
   "Pin 3 (orange) goes to column 9 (red cathode resistor), pin 5 (green) to column 11 (green cathode) and pin 6 (blue) to column 12 (blue cathode). The wire ends are in rows d, c and b of the bottom half.",
   "The sketch comment says 'Anode: GND', but the manual text and images connect the common anode to 5V. I followed the text and images."
  ]
 },
